Name in Reference” as given in the source of the occurrence record (see Collection Unit Notes).\\nNODE records include additional metadata such as environmental classifications of sites and taxonomic/nomenclatural comments that are being prepared for future import to Neotoma.","recdatecreated":"2026-02-14T00:39:47"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":38441,"sitename":"Tjoto (Tjotta) + ","sitedescription":null,"sitenotes":"Validation status: amber(see Dataset Notes)","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[12.41667,65.83333]}","altitude":null,"collectionunitid":51932,"collectionunit":"NODE-R3716","handle":"NODE-R3716","unittype":"Modern","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/9kxb-jv16"],"agerange":[],"database":"Nonmarine Ostracod Distribution in Europe Database","datasetid":70474,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"G.O.","contactid":9023,"firstname":"Georg Ossian","familyname":"Sars","contactname":"Sars, Georg Ossian"}],"datasettype":"ostracode surface sample","datasetnotes":"This Ostracoda dataset was uploaded as part of the bulk import of NODE (Non-marine Ostracod Distribution in Europe) to Neotoma in 2026, using the DataBUS upload system (https://github.com/NeotomaDB/DataBUS). This database import was coordinated by Alison Smith, David Horne, Robin Smith, Andrew Anderson, Simon Goring, Socorro Dominguez, and Jack Williams. David Horne is the lead steward for the NODE database which was originally established by members of the EU Human Capital and Mobility Programme project “Evolutionary ecology of reproductive modes in non-marine Ostracoda” (1994-1996), primarily to enable mapping of sexual and parthenogenetic reproductive modes.  Further development of NODE has included continued data entry, application of taxonomic revisions, and validation exercises using Google Earth and other online resources to check, correct and refine the coordinates of every record. Each record is assigned a Validation Status colour: green (a